            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0563" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 15778/80.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Squiers to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-07-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Squiers reports that the Government of Panama agrees to demands of the United
                    States in the <hi rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Buffalo</hi> cases. Says an indemnity of $5,000 will be paid in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi> case; offers to pay $8,000 indemnity to
                    the relatives of Rand and $1,000 to Cieslik in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Buffalo</hi> cases, and will dismiss, by presidential decree, all police
                    officers who were present at time of disturbance in case of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Buffalo</hi>. Asks instructions.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
